```

This assert statement will check if the last index of the value 'x' in the old list is different from the last index of the value 'x' in the new list. If they are the same, or if any of the original list methods failed (for example, it's invalid to insert an item at an index greater than the list's current count), then your program will terminate execution and provide a stack trace back to the point where the assertion failed.

Please note that `Debug.Assert` is used for testing and development purposes only. It does not have the same effect as `assert` in a release build. It is primarily used to check conditions that should never be false while the program is in development, or testing phase. For production-level code, you'd want to use regular if statements and proper error handling.
